{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:KnotsParticlesConfinement.ElectroweakTripletFarCommutingMinimal","@type":"LeanModule","name":"KnotsParticlesConfinement.ElectroweakTripletFarCommutingMinimal","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.electroweak_triplet_far_commuting_minimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.electroweak_triplet_far_commuting_minimal","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-far-commuting-minimal.lean#L103-L130","doc":"**Theorem — electroweak triplet far-commuting minimality.**\n\nThree pairwise far-commuting even-twist `2`-component torus-link\ngenerators `σ_a, σ_b, σ_c` (`1 ≤ a`, pairwise gap `≥ 2`)\n\n1. require at least `6` strands (`6 ≤ strandsFor c`), attained *uniquely*\n   by `(a, b, c) = (1, 3, 5)` in `B_6`; and\n\n2. the nontrivial strictly-sub-saturating even-twist links (Seifert genus\n   `g` with `1 ≤ g ≤ 3`) are exactly `{T(2,4), T(2,6), T(2,8)}`\n   (`k ∈ {2,3,4}`).\n\nBoth halves are elementary `ℕ`-arithmetic, Lean-proved sorry-free. The\n`n = 6` minimality is physically realised by the three disjoint\nstrand-pairs of `thm:hoefsmit-ew-cell-content`; the enumeration is the\ncanonical `ew_enumeration` of `prop:electroweak-triplet-bring-embedding`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:ew-triplet-far-commuting-minimal","label":"thm:ew-triplet-far-commuting-minimal","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-far-commuting-minimal.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.sub_saturating_enumeration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.sub_saturating_enumeration","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-far-commuting-minimal.lean#L92-L99","doc":"**Sub-saturating enumeration.** The even-twist links `T(2, 2k)` whose\nSeifert genus lies strictly between the Hopf endpoint and the genus-`4`\nBring saturation — `1 ≤ g ≤ 3` — are *exactly* `k ∈ {2, 3, 4}`, i.e. the\ntriplet `T(2,4), T(2,6), T(2,8)`. This is the sorry-free `ew_enumeration`\nof the sibling proposition, reproduced inline (self-containment note). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.torusLinkGenus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.torusLinkGenus","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-far-commuting-minimal.lean#L88-L90","doc":"Seifert genus of the even `2`-component torus link `T(2, 2k)`: `g = k − 1`\n(identical to `torusLinkGenus` of `prop:electroweak-triplet-bring-embedding`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.far_commuting_min_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.far_commuting_min_witness","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-far-commuting-minimal.lean#L68-L84","doc":"**The consecutive odd triple `(1, 3, 5)` realises the minimum.** It is\nfar-commuting, its top index is `5`, and it fits in `B_6`\n(`strandsFor 5 = 6`); moreover among far-commuting triples it is the\n*unique* one attaining `strandsFor c = 6` (any far-commuting triple with\n`c + 1 = 6` must be `(1, 3, 5)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.far_commuting_min_strands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.far_commuting_min_strands","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-far-commuting-minimal.lean#L61-L66","doc":"**Minimum strand count.** Under the same far-commuting hypotheses, the\nthree generators fit only in `B_n` with `n = strandsFor c ≥ 6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.far_commuting_top_index_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.far_commuting_top_index_ge","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-far-commuting-minimal.lean#L53-L59","doc":"**Far-commuting lower bound.** Three positive generator indices\n`a < b < c` that are pairwise *far-commuting* (pairwise gap `≥ 2`,\nencoded `a + 2 ≤ b` and `b + 2 ≤ c` with `1 ≤ a`) force the top index\n`c ≥ 5`. Hence they need at least `strandsFor c = c + 1 ≥ 6` strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.strandsFor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.strandsFor","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-triplet-far-commuting-minimal.lean#L49-L51","doc":"Number of strands a braid generator `σ_i` (index `i`) lives in: `σ_i`\nacts on strands `i, i+1` of `B_{i+1}`, i.e. needs `i + 1` strands. ","signatureChunk":0}]}